The `_session/steering` extension for the DeepSeek Harness ACP adapter.

The harness agent loop already has the three primitives (followup, steer,
inject); its ACP bridge exposed none of them, so a running DeepSeek turn
could not be steered and every RET only queued for the next turn. This
patch gives the bridge the same extension claude-code-acp carries: it
advertises `_meta.steering.supported` at initialize and answers
`_session/steering` by admitting the content and handing it to
`agent.steer()`, which the loop takes at its next step boundary. An idle
session answers `promptRequired`, which is the outcome the ACP backend
(lib/compos/core/agent/backend/acp.ex) turns back into a queued prompt.

The adapter is an npm build, so `npm install` in ~/src/dsh-acp drops this.
Replay it with:

  cd ~/src/dsh-acp/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh-acp
  patch -p1 < ~/src/compos/docs/dsh-acp-steering.patch

